  <main id="main-content" class="guide-main" style="--accent:#15803D;--accent-soft:#DCFCE7;--accent-border:#BBF7D0;">
    <div class="container guide-layout">
      <article class="guide-card">
        <div class="guide-label">PipelineSync resource</div>
        <h2>Use it to make the next step clearer</h2>
        <p class="intro">Governance keeps a HubSpot portal understandable, safe, and ready to change. Use this checklist before a new build, after a migration, or during a quarterly portal review to make sure the system is still supporting the business it serves.</p>
        <section><h3>Access and permissions</h3><p>Start with who can see, edit, export, and delete information. Permission design should match responsibilities without creating unnecessary barriers for the people doing the work.</p><ul><li>Review teams, permission sets, and super-admin access.</li><li>Confirm sensitive properties and export permissions are restricted.</li><li>Test access using representative user roles, not only an administrator account.</li></ul></section><section><h3>Data model and validation</h3><p>A clean data model makes the correct action easier. Check that objects, properties, associations, and required values have a clear purpose and consistent definition.</p><ul><li>Remove duplicate or unused properties.</li><li>Document property owners, definitions, formats, and allowed values.</li><li>Confirm validation rules protect reporting without blocking legitimate work.</li></ul></section><section><h3>Naming and audit trails</h3><p>Consistent naming lets teams find the right asset quickly and makes troubleshooting possible. Every important change should have enough context for another administrator to understand it later.</p><ul><li>Apply naming conventions to properties, workflows, lists, views, and dashboards.</li><li>Record the owner, purpose, and last review date for critical assets.</li><li>Review change history, inactive assets, and unowned workflows.</li></ul></section>
        <section>
          <h3>Resource checklist</h3>
          <p>Use these checkpoints to turn the template into a working process.</p>
          <div class="guide-checklist"><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Permission sets reviewed</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Super-admin access justified</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Property catalogue current</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Validation rules tested</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Naming conventions applied</div></div><div class="guide-check"><span>✓</span><div>Audit trail owners assigned</div></div></div>
        </section>
        <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Governance is not a pile of restrictions. It is the shared system that keeps a portal usable, explainable, and safe as more people and processes depend on it.</p></div>
